WEBVTT

00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:10.900
Welcome home, Matthew.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:15.710
I'm back. There was a letter from Anne.

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:16.940
From Anne?

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:18.370
Yes, Marilla.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:22.310
Would you read it to me, please?
I wonder what she might have written.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:27.340
Don't rush me.
My eyes have not been good recently.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.650
It's difficult to read small letters.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:37.070
As expected, she cannot come home
until the graduation exam this spring is over.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.530
Not until spring...

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.570
After the Christmas holidays, the students from Avonlea

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:50.220
have given up coming home every Friday
in order to study diligently.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:53.900
Though the main reason is their
preparations for the graduation exam,

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:58.070
another reason is that traffic is
inconvenienced because of the snow.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.490
"I had intended to come home at
least one weekend to help you out,

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:09.760
"but I must dedicate myself to studying
so that I can graduate with honors.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:13.830
"I want to be able to come
back home with pride,

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:17.530
"so please forgive me for my selfish ways.

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:21.800
"Please take care of yourselves during the cold season."

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:31.800
There's still five months until
the graduation exam, Matthew.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.610
Well, now...

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:37.030
If everyone's working that hard,
then she doesn't have a choice.

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:43.040
But it would do her good to
come home and relax sometimes.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:45.780
She's putting too much effort into it.
It's not good.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.520
Well, now...

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:52.660
I don't mean to complain,
but five months is a long time.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.000
Right.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:04:00.250
To Matthew and Marilla, who have been
looking forward to Anne's visits every Friday,

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:06.200
the winter that Anne doesn't come home
to visit seems extraordinarily long.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:11.510
Anne is studying very hard.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.770
Although she doesn't reveal this
to those around her,

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:15.970
she's secretly competing with Gilbert,

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.800
just as intensely as she used
to do at Avonlea school.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:24.480
But the feelings she had in the past
has faded away for some reason.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:31.620
Rather than to beat Gilbert, she now
treats him as a good rival.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:57.340
Yes?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:00.420
It's almost one o'clock.
Isn't it time for you to go to bed?

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.650
I'm sorry. I'll just finish this,
and then I will go to sleep.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.550
You mustn't overdo it.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.570
If you damage your health,
it'll all be for nothing.

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:10.960
Yes.

00:05:29.950 --> 00:05:31.840
Come on, Gilbert!

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:38.820
Take that!

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.860
Come on! Do your best!

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:48.700
Being handsome has its rewards.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:51.090
If you hit, it's 'Oh!' and if you fall, it's 'Ah!'

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.430
Right. Ouch!

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.520
Yesterday, in the teacher's room,

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:00.780
I heard that they have chosen three
candidates for the gold medal this year.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.440
Who are those three?

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.590
The first must be Gilbert Blythe, right?

00:06:04.610 --> 00:06:08.180
I don't know the ranking,
but it's Gilbert, Lewis Wilson,

00:06:08.190 --> 00:06:10.840
and one more. It's you, Anne Shirley.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:13.120
That's a good ranking, isn't it?

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:16.260
But as a girl, I want Anne to get the prize.

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.810
Me, too. Anne, you can't disappoint us.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.050
I won't. But it will be very difficult to beat Gilbert.

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.410
The honor and glory of all the
female students at Queen's

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:29.200
now rests on your shoulders, Anne Shirley.

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.980
Can I really shoulder such a heavy responsibility?

00:06:32.020 --> 00:06:34.450
How can we win with
all that negativity?

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.050
It's the responsibility of the chosen
to advance toward victory!

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:41.820
Oh! Why is life so unfair?

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.700
While Anne's talking about first place,

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.550
we're wondering if we will
be able to graduate, right?

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:52.090
Oh, but you're the prettiest girl at Queen's.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:55.480
However, you are the prettiest
in the advanced level.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:58.000
And Jane's an honor
student of home economics.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:00.520
What is the big deal with being first?

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.320
Oh! You didn't know? You have the
honor of being number one, too.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:11.990
Josie Pye, you have the honor of
being the meanest of all the girls here.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:16.290
Stella Maynard! It's not an honor to be called that!

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.790
Oh, is that so?

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:37.070
Come, come. You mustn't make such a racket.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:45.180
Come, come.

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:49.250
You're just feeling lonely
because you can't see Anne.

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:56.800
But Anne won't be coming
back until it's spring.

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:01.230
Come, come. Yes, yes.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:17.750
Matthew, what's wrong?

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:19.570
Matthew!

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.920
Hold on, Matthew. Matthew!

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:29.400
Should we send a telegram to Anne?

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.480
It's not that I think something
bad is going to happen to Matthew,

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:38.520
but this winter cold can't
be good for his heart.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:41.290
How can I ask her to come home?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.080
What?

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:46.140
Anne has begun her final studies.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.420
That's what she said in her letter.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.570
She seems so enthusiastic and lively,

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.580
and this is not the first time
Matthew has had an attack.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.520
That's true, but I still feel,

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:02.320
now is not the time to be studying.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:08.160
No. There's no need to
send for Anne, Mrs. Lynde.

00:09:08.450 --> 00:09:09.600
Matthew.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:12.700
Brother, you have to lie
down a little longer.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:17.580
No, I'm all right now.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:21.030
If we send for her every
time I get an attack,

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:24.210
she won't be able to
concentrate on her studies.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.740
There's no need for that, Marilla.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:28.790
I know, Matthew.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:33.690
But you know, Matthew, that it's very
hard for Marilla when you're sick.

00:09:33.730 --> 00:09:36.280
She has to take care of the
livestock and chop wood, and...

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:37.900
It's all right.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:43.610
No, I have raised more than ten
children. I can see you love her.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:46.200
But a girl should...

00:09:46.820 --> 00:09:49.340
We mustn't send for Anne.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.210
It's not fair to Marilla,
but we can hire someone,

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.830
and I can still work.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:59.240
Anyway, you mustn't send for Anne.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:01.020
Oh dear.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:05.460
I knew both of you would
be stubborn about this,

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.260
but I didn't know you placed so much
emphasis on education.

00:10:09.510 --> 00:10:15.000
While he can maintain stubbornness,
I guess he's still healthy enough.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.430
On Sundays,

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.510
Anne pays Miss Barry a visit at Beechwood,
and they go to church together.

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:34.510
Since she's so busy studying these days,
this gives her an opportunity to have some fun.

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:39.780
By the way, Anne, is Matthew's condition any better?

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.320
Condition?

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:43.080
His heart.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.780
What? What's wrong with Matthew's heart?

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.560
What's wrong, you say...

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.540
Didn't he fall down in a heart attack recently?

00:10:51.220 --> 00:10:53.150
No one told you about this?

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.440
Matthew has had heart problems and
he's had seizures quite often, right?

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:04.940
Oh my. It seems you didn't know about this.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.150
What is going on?

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.920
Miss Barry, please tell me more.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:13.100
What's wrong with Matthew's heart?
What condition does he have?

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:17.260
Even if you ask me, I'm not too sure myself.

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:22.270
They said he has a weak heart.
Since he's old, that's only expected.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:23.660
A weak heart!

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:28.840
Since no one has informed you,
I don't think it's very serious.

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:32.670
Still, those two are really great people.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.620
They actually kept this from you,
so as not to worry you.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.520
Anne, calm down.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:46.700
You shouldn't worry about Matthew.
Anyway, please sit down and finish your meal.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:51.170
Hearing that Matthew has always had a weak heart,

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.250
Anne berates herself for not noticing it before.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:12:01.660
She suspects that Matthew has kept the
truth from her so as not to worry her.

00:12:02.780 --> 00:12:06.340
Just thinking about it
makes her uncomfortable.

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.180
Anne! What in the world...?!

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.880
Why are you coming home suddenly
without letting us know?

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:50.810
You surprised me!

00:13:51.020 --> 00:13:54.290
Marilla, it's awful. Why didn't you tell me?

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.290
Tell you what? Is something wrong at school?

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:58.730
About Matthew.

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.050
Matthew is in bed because
of his weak heart, isn't he?

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:05.030
So it's about that.
Who told you?

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.820
Miss Barry told me Matthew
has been sick for some time,

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.320
and that he fell down in a heart attack.

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:15.570
And I went to Queen's blithely
without knowing anything!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.430
I... I...!

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:23.510
Now, now. Don't get so excited.
I'm sorry for not telling you.

00:14:23.720 --> 00:14:28.320
Matthew isn't sick in bed.
There's no need to worry.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.840
Anyway, please sit down.
It's cold outside, isn't it?

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.150
Where is Matthew?

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:33.420
In his room.

00:14:34.730 --> 00:14:37.390
Matthew. Matthew!

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.960
Matthew, how is your condition?

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:41.270
I heard that it's been bad for some time.
Is it serious?

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:47.260
Anne, welcome home. I'm all right.
Look at me. I'm still as strong as ever.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:49.070
Matthew. Matthew!

00:14:50.810 --> 00:14:54.820
She heard about your condition
and came back home in a hurry.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:59.390
Well, when Miss Barry told me,
my heart almost stopped beating!

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:03.360
My heart almost stopped, too, when I
saw you walk in from that storm.

00:15:03.620 --> 00:15:05.050
Well, now.

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:10.200
One person with a heart
condition is more than enough.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.700
Well, that's quite true.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:15.700
Well, I was very surprised.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.370
It's been two months since the
three of us were gathered.

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:23.200
Well, now. You've really
come home now, Anne.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.390
That's because I heard you had fallen down.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:36.160
But having a weak heart
is scary, right? Does it hurt?

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:41.490
Yes. It is awful when it starts
acting up again,

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:44.430
but it gets better very quickly.

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.440
Have you seen a doctor?

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:47.370
At times.

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.770
That will not do.
You must see a doctor regularly.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:56.470
The doctor said it was not life-threatening.

00:15:57.070 --> 00:15:59.030
I am getting old, Anne.

00:15:59.110 --> 00:16:02.640
It's only natural that something
like this would happen.

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:05.400
Don't worry too much.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:11.620
We kept it from you only because
we didn't want you to worry.

00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:16.240
The best medicine for Matthew's heart, Anne,

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:19.930
is for you continue to study diligently.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:21.550
- Right, Matthew?
- Yes.

00:16:21.950 --> 00:16:24.480
However, we are very happy

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:27.540
that you came home because
you were worried about Matthew.

00:16:28.180 --> 00:16:29.740
Yes.

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.460
I understand.

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:33.980
Anne's sudden return

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:38.840
brings a small happiness to the
two lonely people at Green Gables.

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:44.550
Matthew and Marilla enjoy a long-awaited
family gathering once again.

00:16:45.710 --> 00:16:50.870
When Anne returns to Charlottetown,
she studies even harder than before.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:56.450
Then, almost before anybody
has realized it, spring has come.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.620
"Dear Diana, how are you?

00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:04.850
"Although I'm in Charlottetown,

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.980
"I'm thinking about Lovers' Lane,

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.740
"Snow Queen, the Birch Path
and the Violet Vale in Avonlea.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:15.550
"Spring is in the air, and I feel
the new season is coming."

00:18:16.100 --> 00:18:18.560
"I heard that your birthday party was very nice.

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:22.440
"I feel bad not being able to be there
to offer my blessings.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:26.750
"Although the graduation exam is
just round the corner,

00:18:26.820 --> 00:18:30.440
"I'm not going to worry about it.
I'm just going to try my best.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.850
"With this letter,
I'm sending you a glass brooch

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:36.070
"which would look lovely on you.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:42.460
"Although it's a little late,
Happy Birthday nonetheless.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:45.460
"Your bosom friend, Anne Shirley."

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:10.570
Oh! I can't stand it anymore.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:15.560
If it were not for mathematics,
I would enjoy life much more.

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.020
I agree.

00:19:17.060 --> 00:19:19.390
It's no use crying about it now.

00:19:19.430 --> 00:19:21.230
Go on. You must do it.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:24.550
The students who are preparing
for the graduation exam

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:28.160
cannot afford to enjoy the coming of spring.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:32.210
I can't believe that this
semester is coming to an end.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.720
Don't say that so carelessly!

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.690
Everyone!

00:19:38.010 --> 00:19:40.250
Sometimes I feel as if the
exam means everything,

00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.210
but I can't help feeling that
it's a waste to stay inside

00:19:43.230 --> 00:19:45.720
when I look at the big buds swelling
on those chestnut trees,

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:50.460
and the misty blue air
at the end of the streets.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:52.530
Then the exam doesn't seem
to matter that much.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.090
Doesn't seem to matter?!

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.710
And of course the sky is misty when spring arrives.

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:04.730
Anne, you say that so carelessly since
you're certain of passing the graduation exams.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.740
As for us, being able to pass
it is a serious issue.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:11.070
At the very least,
I don't want to fail.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:14.500
We can't regard this philosophically.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:15.560
That's right!

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.040
I've lost seven pounds
in the last two weeks.

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:21.380
It's no use to say don't worry.

00:20:21.380 --> 00:20:22.610
I WILL worry.

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.410
And worrying helps you some.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:29.820
It seems as if you were doin
something when you're worrying.

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:34.590
We've been here at Queen's all winter,
and has spent a lot of money.

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:36.800
It would be terrible if we didn't get our licenses.

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.650
In that respect, I am okay.

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:41.180
If I don't pass this year,
I'm coming back next.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:44.110
My father can afford to send me.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.120
By the way, Anne, Frank Stockley
told me that Professor Tremaine

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:51.560
said that it's certain that
Gilbert Blythe will take the gold medal,

00:20:51.590 --> 00:20:56.680
and that Emily Clay would likely
win the Avery scholarship.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.160
Your name wasn't mentioned at all.

00:21:00.540 --> 00:21:04.720
That may make me feel badly tomorrow, Josie,

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.800
but as long as I know the violets

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.500
are coming out all purple down in
the hollow below Green Gables,

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:14.510
and that little ferns are poking
their heads up in Lovers' Lane,

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:19.420
it's not a great deal of difference
whether I win the Avery or not.

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:26.500
I've done my best and I begin to understand
what is meant by the 'joy of the strife.'

00:21:28.320 --> 00:21:34.800
Next to trying and winning,
the best thing is trying and failing.

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:38.510
Everyone, let's not study anymore today.

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:42.530
Look at that arch of pale,
green, sky over those houses,

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.580
and picture to yourself what it must look like

00:21:46.590 --> 00:21:50.950
over the purply-dark
beech-woods back of Avonlea.

00:21:51.600 --> 00:21:53.270
I'm just not in the mood.

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:58.420
I keep imagining that my name
won't be on the the pass list.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.930
It's enough to make me burst into tears.

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:05.260
I'm certain I will cry, too,
if that happens to me.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.760
And so, at last, the day of the graduation exam arrives.

00:22:48.550 --> 00:22:51.580
Anne! How did you do on the exam?

00:22:51.610 --> 00:22:56.130
I passed Gilbert in the hallway just now.
He seemed confident.

00:22:56.350 --> 00:22:57.390
Anne, what about you?

00:22:57.780 --> 00:23:00.160
Well, I'm leaving this in God's hands.

00:23:00.620 --> 00:23:05.780
I didn't know half of the Math. I'm sure
what I was afraid of will come true.

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:09.670
There's nothing to worry about.
If you fail, there's one more year left.

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:13.950
What a beautiful sunset.

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:24.880
Ruby, do you know what you are going to
wear for the graduation ceremony?

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:29.520
Yes. My mom sent me a letter,
saying she's going to order

00:23:29.560 --> 00:23:33.460
a white dress from a tailor in Carmody,
and asked me for my measurements.

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:35.850
But that's only if I graduate.

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:40.810
I have ordered three gowns
from the tailors here in town.

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.740
I intend to wear the best one.

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:46.840
Do you think I should wear my light-blue dress?

00:23:46.880 --> 00:23:51.650
It was made last spring, but I really
want to wear it. It's my favourite.

00:23:52.720 --> 00:23:56.590
Anne doesn't worry about what she's
going to wear for the graduation ceremony.

00:23:58.490 --> 00:24:03.930
She's immersed in the pleasant
tiredness after the battle.

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:06.090
In the waning sunset,

00:24:06.130 --> 00:24:10.230
she's dreaming of all the hope and
possibilities that await her in the future.

00:24:18.940 --> 00:24:21.100
Once the grueling graduation exams are over,

00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:25.240
the winners of the gold medal
and Avery scholarship will be announced

00:24:25.500 --> 00:24:28.350
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 45

00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:29.880
The Glory and the Dream

00:24:29.980 --> 00:24:31.130
Please look forward to it!
